1
00:00:00,500 --> 00:00:01,719
P/B.

2
00:00:01,919 --> 00:00:03,069
Price to Book.

3
00:00:03,269 --> 00:00:05,356
This one does not care about profit.

4
00:00:05,556 --> 00:00:09,342
It asks a simpler question: what is the company worth on paper,

5
00:00:09,342 --> 00:00:13,578
if you added up everything it owns and paid off everything it owes?

6
00:00:14,328 --> 00:00:15,762
Open the balance sheet.

7
00:00:15,962 --> 00:00:19,646
On one side, everything the company owns: cash, factories,

8
00:00:19,646 --> 00:00:21,829
inventory, money customers owe.

9
00:00:22,029 --> 00:00:24,014
Say five hundred crore of assets.

10
00:00:24,214 --> 00:00:28,033
On the other side, everything it owes: loans and unpaid bills.

11
00:00:28,233 --> 00:00:29,837
Say three hundred crore.

12
00:00:30,587 --> 00:00:33,056
Assets minus liabilities is book value,

13
00:00:33,056 --> 00:00:36,561
also called shareholders' equity: two hundred crore.

14
00:00:36,761 --> 00:00:39,274
That is the accountant's answer to the question,

15
00:00:39,274 --> 00:00:40,943
what is left for the owners.

16
00:00:41,693 --> 00:00:43,298
Divide by ten crore shares,

17
00:00:43,298 --> 00:00:46,003
and book value per share is twenty rupees.

18
00:00:46,203 --> 00:00:47,800
The share price is forty.

19
00:00:47,999 --> 00:00:51,285
So P/B is forty over twenty, which is two.

20
00:00:52,036 --> 00:00:55,859
A P/B of two means the market pays two rupees for every

21
00:00:55,859 --> 00:00:58,650
one rupee of net assets on the books.

22
00:00:58,850 --> 00:00:59,383
Below one,

23
00:00:59,383 --> 00:01:02,520
you are buying assets for less than their stated value.

24
00:01:02,720 --> 00:01:05,763
That is either a bargain, or the market thinks those assets

25
00:01:05,763 --> 00:01:08,028
are not really worth what the books say.

26
00:01:08,778 --> 00:01:12,287
Where it shines: banks, insurers, and asset-heavy businesses,

27
00:01:12,287 --> 00:01:14,795
where the balance sheet is the business.

28
00:01:14,995 --> 00:01:18,294
Where it fails: software or brands, whose real value,

29
00:01:18,294 --> 00:01:21,308
people and ideas, never shows up as an asset.

30
00:01:21,508 --> 00:01:23,869
And always pair it with return on equity.

31
00:01:24,069 --> 00:01:27,721
A company earning twenty percent on its book deserves a

32
00:01:27,721 --> 00:01:30,128
higher P/B than one earning five.

